# Runtime output, never committed.
#
# `pa.py` no longer writes here -- since the SNAPSHOT_DIR fix it writes to
# `~/.pa-api-cache/snapshots`, outside any checkout and outside the installed
# plugin, so no ignore rule is load-bearing for it any more.
#
# This rule stays as a net, not as documentation. Two earlier versions of that
# constant DID write into a repo: a CWD-relative path put live-tenant dumps at
# whatever directory pa.py was launched from, and an anchor on `__file__` put
# them right here. A checkout that ran either still has the directory, and the
# rule is what keeps it out of a commit.
#
# What those files are, and why it matters: a verbatim dump of a live tenant --
# environment and flow GUIDs, connection references, SharePoint site URLs, and
# whatever the flow's own actions embed. One was committed and pushed to this
# PUBLIC repo before anyone noticed, found by a review rather than by a person
# reading the diff, because a 51KB JSON blob in a 59-file changeset is exactly
# what nobody opens.
scripts/pa-snapshots/
